WEBVTT

01:48.360 --> 01:49.580
Father...

01:51.410 --> 01:52.510
<i>Why?</i>

01:52.920 --> 01:55.880
<i>Why are you looking at me like that?</i>

01:56.310 --> 01:57.520
<i>Father...</i>

01:58.470 --> 02:03.470
<b>The Samurai and the Woman</b>

02:01.990 --> 02:04.900
You're awake, Sagiri.

02:05.260 --> 02:06.660
Genji-dono.

02:06.930 --> 02:08.660
Where are we?

02:08.660 --> 02:10.150
What happened to me?

02:10.490 --> 02:12.470
We're in a cavern on the island.

02:12.970 --> 02:15.650
I sense no monsters or insects in the area.

02:16.350 --> 02:20.990
You were poisoned by the butterflies' 
scales and lost consciousness.

02:23.550 --> 02:25.620
You shouldn't move around yet.

02:26.120 --> 02:27.170
I can't do that.

02:28.080 --> 02:30.220
I mustn't take my eyes off my prisoner.

02:30.680 --> 02:32.690
Hey, you're awake.

02:32.690 --> 02:33.610
Oh?

02:33.610 --> 02:35.920
How are you feeling, Sagiri-san?

02:37.730 --> 02:40.440
Um, what is all of this?

02:41.630 --> 02:42.880
I'm preparing dinner.

02:42.880 --> 02:45.030
I'm mending our torn clothes.

02:45.030 --> 02:46.180
<i>I'm</i> supervising.

02:46.790 --> 02:49.450
Didn't you say we're short on time?

02:49.450 --> 02:53.320
Well, you know... I had reservations.

02:55.950 --> 02:58.600
Now that Sagiri-san is awake,

02:58.600 --> 03:02.250
why don't we go over what we know together?

03:02.250 --> 03:04.960
We can eat the food 
Gabimaru-san made while we talk.

03:05.580 --> 03:07.080
I'm in.

03:07.080 --> 03:09.590
Hey, these are kikatsugan.

03:09.590 --> 03:12.500
I was hoping for a proper meal.

03:12.500 --> 03:13.840
Kikatsugan?

03:13.840 --> 03:16.330
I made them using stuff in the area.

03:16.330 --> 03:18.090
I think they're actually pretty well made.

03:18.310 --> 03:22.890
And while I was out gathering ingredients, 
I scouted out the island.

03:24.310 --> 03:29.470
To cut to the chase, I didn't see 
anything promising in the area.

03:29.470 --> 03:32.320
Though since we don't know what 
the whole island looks like,

03:32.320 --> 03:33.860
I can't speak much on the subject.

03:33.860 --> 03:37.120
Would you be able to recognize 
it even if it were around?

03:37.120 --> 03:39.250
Do you know something 
about the Elixir of Life?

03:43.070 --> 03:43.990
No.

03:43.990 --> 03:46.660
This job was the first I heard 
about the Elixir of Life.

03:47.160 --> 03:49.110
I searched based on the drawing we have.

03:49.900 --> 03:51.620
Huh.

03:53.620 --> 03:56.950
What I learned while gathering 
ingredients was about the flora.

03:57.260 --> 04:01.900
The species are mixed, but they're mostly 
ordinary plants found on the mainland.

04:02.310 --> 04:04.890
I saw a few unfamiliar ones, too.

04:05.240 --> 04:08.610
We're near Ryukyu. 
They could be flowers from there.

04:08.610 --> 04:11.510
Wow, awesome.

04:11.760 --> 04:13.100
What caught my attention was that

04:13.100 --> 04:16.030
I found several flowers resembling 
the samurai who had become flowers.

04:16.030 --> 04:16.540
What?

04:16.540 --> 04:17.530
Could it be?

04:17.530 --> 04:20.510
Where did the samurai sent here go?

04:21.040 --> 04:24.290
If most of the plants 
on this island used to be humans,

04:25.080 --> 04:26.990
then we can guess what happened to them.

04:29.300 --> 04:31.190
How could you feed that to us?!

04:31.190 --> 04:33.300
I didn't use anything like that.

04:33.520 --> 04:37.550
In any case, I didn't find anything 
like this mandarin-looking thing.

04:37.550 --> 04:41.260
Perhaps we shouldn't fixate 
on the illustration too much.

04:41.790 --> 04:45.350
The terms "Tokijiku no Kagunomi" 
and "Paradise" used

04:45.350 --> 04:48.180
by the shogunate were originally concepts 
from different cultures.

04:48.740 --> 04:50.270
The stone statues scattered around

04:50.270 --> 04:52.560
the island closely resemble 
Buddhist or Taoist figures.

04:52.560 --> 04:55.820
Worrying about religious 
consistency might be a waste of time.

04:55.830 --> 04:59.200
What we should be focusing 
on is the statues themselves.

04:59.200 --> 05:02.830
Does the technology to create stone 
or clay figures exist on the island?

05:02.830 --> 05:05.040
If so, then who made them?

05:05.040 --> 05:08.330
Do they even live here?

05:09.110 --> 05:12.830
I find it hard to believe 
people could live on this island.

05:13.190 --> 05:16.670
Both the monsters and insects 
are too dangerous for humans.

05:16.670 --> 05:19.000
Their ecology and behavior are mysterious.

05:19.010 --> 05:20.350
When I cut them,

05:20.960 --> 05:25.630
it felt as though they had flesh 
and bones, but organs and, um...

05:27.370 --> 05:28.620
Reproductive organs?

05:29.010 --> 05:31.360
Yes. I didn't see any.

05:31.360 --> 05:33.360
So they don't have dicks.

05:34.730 --> 05:36.760
Their appearance is strange as well.

05:36.760 --> 05:41.350
Parts of other animals 
are stacked on top of humanoid forms.

05:41.350 --> 05:43.430
I'm not sure how to describe it.

05:43.430 --> 05:44.860
I know what you mean.

05:44.860 --> 05:48.520
The items worn by the monsters 
seem poorly-made as well.

05:48.520 --> 05:52.150
They're religious, 
but the details are crude.

05:52.470 --> 05:53.870
In other words...

05:54.350 --> 05:56.650
They're like malformed gods.

05:56.650 --> 05:59.110
Both the island and monsters are like that.

05:59.110 --> 06:01.310
They're terrifying, but they're also stupid.

06:01.920 --> 06:04.990
Too unrealistic to be natural.

06:04.990 --> 06:08.380
Too artificial to be mystical.

06:09.020 --> 06:13.420
It's as though we've been thrown 
into some kind of sick mandala.

06:14.690 --> 06:18.480
They're so mysterious, 
we can't begin to understand them.

06:24.940 --> 06:29.700
Creatures that can survive 
without organs point to immortality.

06:29.700 --> 06:33.150
It's starting to seem possible 
the Elixir of Life is on the island.

06:33.150 --> 06:35.100
And if it's here, then it can be found.

06:35.550 --> 06:37.930
If we find it, we can be pardoned.

06:38.930 --> 06:44.060
Unless we're already dead, 
and this place is the real afterlife.

06:44.060 --> 06:47.190
I certainly hope that's not the case.

06:47.190 --> 06:49.140
Gabimaru-san is right.

06:49.140 --> 06:52.990
We should begin by examining 
the monsters' ecology.

06:52.990 --> 06:55.810
Where and how do the monsters live?

06:55.810 --> 07:00.430
It will be dangerous, but that's currently 
our only clue regarding the Elixir.

07:04.200 --> 07:05.380
<i>Sunset...</i>

07:05.610 --> 07:07.940
<i>It hasn't yet been a full day 
since we arrived on the island.</i>

07:12.250 --> 07:13.710
Genji-dono?

07:14.000 --> 07:17.330
Sagiri, you should take 
a boat back to the mainland.

07:17.880 --> 07:18.730
What are you—

07:18.730 --> 07:20.600
I shall assume your responsibilities.

07:20.600 --> 07:23.220
My own criminal is dead.

07:23.430 --> 07:26.570
You're a daughter of the Yamada 
clan first and a samurai second.

07:26.570 --> 07:29.720
As a woman, it's your duty to marry 
the next head of the clan.

07:29.970 --> 07:33.110
The shogunate wouldn't object 
to me taking over your role.

07:33.560 --> 07:35.600
In your current condition, you'll die.

07:35.910 --> 07:38.150
Go home, Sagiri.

07:41.740 --> 07:43.590
This is my job.

07:43.890 --> 07:45.870
A warrior's duty is to complete their job.

07:45.870 --> 07:49.500
Your intentions are admirable, 
but face the facts.

07:49.800 --> 07:53.190
Do you currently have 
the strength to kill Gabimaru?

07:54.050 --> 07:55.500
And your sword...

07:55.980 --> 07:57.730
I don't know where you found that.

07:57.730 --> 07:59.260
It just happened to be available, didn't it?

07:59.570 --> 08:01.520
A sword is a warrior's heart.

08:01.770 --> 08:05.700
You've already lost 
the heart of the Yamada clan.

08:06.270 --> 08:09.610
I suppose it's not 
uncommon on the battlefield.

08:09.610 --> 08:12.010
During battle, warriors use 
and discard their weapons.

08:12.010 --> 08:14.270
After all, you can procure 
new ones right there.

08:14.680 --> 08:17.780
Your sword skills are exceptional,

08:17.780 --> 08:21.380
but that's as a sword-tester 
and executioner.

08:21.380 --> 08:25.530
This situation calls for skills in battle.

08:26.090 --> 08:29.950
Exceptional sword skills aren't 
the same as exceptional skill in battle.

08:30.260 --> 08:34.040
You're clearly not strong 
enough for this island.

08:34.360 --> 08:36.090
It's beyond your limits as a woman.

08:37.610 --> 08:40.670
Would it be that easy to return, though?

08:40.950 --> 08:42.020
Senta...

08:42.020 --> 08:45.730
Most samurai sent 
to this island don't return.

08:46.370 --> 08:50.470
Even if you used a boat, 
I'm not sure you'd be able to escape easily.

08:51.130 --> 08:53.360
We need to get away from the island.

08:53.360 --> 08:58.900
We may not be able to see because of this fog, 
but a warrior always advances.

08:54.880 --> 08:58.890
<b>Tameshi-itto-ryu Rank 10
Yamada Asaemon
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hTenza</b>

08:59.990 --> 09:02.890
Why are samurai so stupid?

09:02.890 --> 09:03.910
What?

09:03.910 --> 09:06.010
Read the currents.

09:06.010 --> 09:10.040
You'll just get wet relying 
on brute force and exhaust yourself.

09:10.710 --> 09:12.990
Samurai are captivated 
by things that don't exist.

09:12.990 --> 09:15.080
They don't know how to be smart.

09:15.080 --> 09:16.040
I see.

09:16.040 --> 09:17.870
How informative!

09:17.870 --> 09:21.050
Is that the wisdom of the Sanka?

09:21.050 --> 09:22.690
My grandpa taught it to me.

09:22.690 --> 09:24.800
He said to always reduce inefficiency.

09:25.200 --> 09:30.170
Even if we're able to leave the island, 
I'll be executed if I don't have the Elixir.

09:30.170 --> 09:33.410
Don't worry about that. 
I'll talk to the shogunate for you.

09:33.410 --> 09:34.810
Trust me.

09:35.420 --> 09:40.190
I promise I'll see you 
home safe, Nurugai-kun.

09:40.190 --> 09:45.510
Of all the criminals participating, 
you deserve to live the most.

09:47.220 --> 09:48.320
Look at that.

09:48.320 --> 09:50.110
That must be a shogunate ship.

09:50.110 --> 09:51.460
After all, it's big.

09:51.460 --> 09:53.080
Now we can go home.

09:58.790 --> 10:02.590
They're the shogunate's... No.

10:02.590 --> 10:06.770
Could these be all the ships 
that attempted to leave the island?

10:32.490 --> 10:34.040
Idiot, don't draw your sword!

10:34.040 --> 10:34.910
What?

10:40.660 --> 10:44.160
Most animals are sensitive 
to shining objects and hostility.

10:44.160 --> 10:46.170
If we'd turned back right away...

10:46.170 --> 10:47.450
I couldn't help it!

10:47.450 --> 10:49.930
I don't understand this complicated stuff.

10:54.730 --> 10:56.940
Let's search for a usable ship.

11:01.380 --> 11:02.930
<i>Run, Nurugai.</i>

11:03.380 --> 11:06.450
If you die, the Sanka bloodline will end.

11:07.080 --> 11:09.610
<i>We don't believe in things that don't exist.</i>

11:09.610 --> 11:12.110
<i>B-But I can't help but wonder...</i>

11:12.420 --> 11:14.570
<i>Is this divine punishment?</i>

11:15.720 --> 11:16.580
Hey.

11:16.740 --> 11:19.960
If you're lost, I'll take you 
to the foot of the mountain.

11:20.370 --> 11:22.210
Are you an Emishi?

11:22.430 --> 11:24.710
Then allow me to rest in your village.

11:25.380 --> 11:27.070
What's an Emishi?

11:27.830 --> 11:30.040
One who doesn't obey.

11:30.040 --> 11:32.660
A term for those who refuse 
to submit to the shogunate

11:32.660 --> 11:34.950
and live as unique 
cultures in the mountains.

11:35.990 --> 11:38.850
Under Tokugawa-sama's rule, 
they're considered insurrectionists.

11:40.180 --> 11:41.440
Take him away.

11:41.440 --> 11:44.440
He'll be executed once we get the locations 
of the other villages out of him.

11:44.740 --> 11:47.600
Then all the Sanka in this 
region will be eradicated.

11:48.240 --> 11:50.010
<i>I'm sorry, guys.</i>

11:50.010 --> 11:51.690
<i>I'm sorry, Grandpa.</i>

11:52.100 --> 11:54.710
<i>It's all because I brought 
the samurai here...</i>

11:55.810 --> 11:56.920
<i>I...</i>

11:59.460 --> 12:01.110
I am an Asaemon.

12:01.590 --> 12:03.690
Though I'm employed by the government,

12:03.700 --> 12:07.360
I don't understand why 
an innocent boy should be executed.

12:07.360 --> 12:11.130
If there's a way for you to live, 
then you should live.

12:11.980 --> 12:14.870
<i>What should I do?</i>

12:15.240 --> 12:18.250
<i>Should I live so the village's 
bloodline doesn't end?</i>

12:18.630 --> 12:22.140
<i>Or should I die to atone for the villagers?</i>

12:23.050 --> 12:24.070
<i>I...</i>

12:33.420 --> 12:35.650
Kisho-san, why?

12:35.650 --> 12:38.510
It's me, Tenza. Don't you recognize me?

12:38.510 --> 12:41.040
Don't bother. It's too late for him.

12:51.430 --> 12:52.870
We're surrounded.

13:02.710 --> 13:04.770
What are you doing, Nurugai-kun?

13:05.270 --> 13:06.770
Forget me.

13:06.770 --> 13:08.830
If you're going to flee, then flee alone.

13:09.780 --> 13:12.280
Forget about me.

13:12.280 --> 13:15.870
What are you talking about? 
I don't understand.

13:15.870 --> 13:21.030
I've been wondering if I should live or die.

13:21.650 --> 13:25.670
I finally get it. This is divine punishment.

13:26.230 --> 13:30.280
For killing Grandpa and the others.

13:32.510 --> 13:34.290
I don't understand.

13:34.290 --> 13:36.240
Why does that mean you have to die?

13:36.240 --> 13:39.550
Samurai are stupid, right? Explain it to me.

13:40.110 --> 13:45.170
The Sanka convention is to live 
for the mountain and the village.

13:45.550 --> 13:51.270
I'm the sole survivor. Everyone else
 died because of me.

13:52.970 --> 13:56.540
I don't get it. What's a convention?

13:56.540 --> 13:58.470
Don't use big words.

13:58.750 --> 13:59.560
What I'm saying is...

14:04.470 --> 14:06.080
I told you to forget about me.

14:07.370 --> 14:10.330
Until you explain it to me...

14:10.670 --> 14:14.830
Until I understand it, I'm not leaving.

14:20.050 --> 14:23.310
I'm nearly at my limit. 
I haven't got much stamina.

14:23.600 --> 14:25.870
Just explain it to me already.

14:25.870 --> 14:27.870
I'm not asking about 
your grandpa or village.

14:27.870 --> 14:30.550
I'm asking if you want to die.

14:34.140 --> 14:36.440
I don't want to die.

14:37.030 --> 14:38.950
I want to go back to the mountains.

14:40.820 --> 14:43.830
Then there's only one thing to do.

14:44.070 --> 14:46.210
Do whatever it takes to survive.

14:46.210 --> 14:48.700
It looks like there's 
a usable boat over there.

14:48.700 --> 14:51.710
We'll break through here and get on that.

14:54.180 --> 14:54.960
Got it.

15:09.750 --> 15:13.740
You're strong, Nurugai-kun. Thank you.

15:14.410 --> 15:16.230
I could say the same thing.

15:16.570 --> 15:21.510
We escaped the monsters for now, 
but we ended up back here.

15:21.510 --> 15:22.640
Yeah.

15:22.640 --> 15:27.250
The currents in this area probably 
all flow back to the island.

15:27.890 --> 15:30.430
Unless we find a current leading outside,

15:30.430 --> 15:32.670
we won't be able to 
return even with the Elixir.

15:32.670 --> 15:34.510
And those monsters...

15:34.510 --> 15:36.510
They're different from the ones 
that were on the island.

15:37.040 --> 15:40.940
The mountain of grounded ships seemed 
to be surrounding the island, too.

15:40.940 --> 15:43.710
There were more than just 
the expeditions sent over the past few years.

15:44.170 --> 15:47.750
We can think once we've 
washed off this blood.

15:49.850 --> 15:52.590
The ships of the samurai who'd 
been turned into flowers returned.

15:52.590 --> 15:55.160
There must be a current leading out.

15:55.160 --> 15:57.270
You're right.

16:00.260 --> 16:01.780
Nurugai-kun...

16:01.780 --> 16:07.710
Your form is rather... 
girlish, you might say...

16:08.040 --> 16:10.150
Girlish? I <i>am</i> a girl.

16:10.150 --> 16:11.170
What?

16:11.170 --> 16:12.310
But... But...

16:12.310 --> 16:13.680
Seriously? No, wait. But...

16:13.680 --> 16:15.410
Why are you so flustered?

16:15.410 --> 16:17.430
Face the other way if you're a girl.

16:17.430 --> 16:21.040
Samurai love to fixate on things 
that don't matter.

16:17.950 --> 16:19.070
Face the other way!

16:21.040 --> 16:23.230
It does matter.

16:23.230 --> 16:25.550
Just face the other way.

16:25.550 --> 16:27.630
I've fallen for your chivalry.

16:27.630 --> 16:29.600
Once we make it back safely, 
let's get married.

16:29.600 --> 16:34.240
All the stuff with the island 
and everything is too much for my brain.

16:34.240 --> 16:35.560
I'm stupid, you see.

16:36.030 --> 16:39.310
In any case, let's 
review what we need to do.

16:39.710 --> 16:44.270
First, we'll circle the island 
and find a current leading out.

16:44.270 --> 16:47.270
We shouldn't do anything 
until we've secured an escape route.

16:47.520 --> 16:51.450
And it's too dangerous for just the two of 
us to try to get through the monsters.

16:51.800 --> 16:54.440
We should gather allies for the return trip.

16:55.130 --> 16:58.240
Once dawn breaks, 
you should sail home, Sagiri.

16:58.700 --> 17:01.960
This job is too much for a woman.

17:03.300 --> 17:03.960
I...

17:03.960 --> 17:06.910
half-agree with Genji-san.

17:06.910 --> 17:10.970
Whatever the reason, you should 
leave this place if you can.

17:11.490 --> 17:14.470
But the other half of me wants you to

17:14.470 --> 17:17.480
be here in case Gabimaru-san 
needs to be stopped.

17:17.640 --> 17:19.880
You do?

17:19.880 --> 17:21.970
It's just a hunch, but...

17:22.350 --> 17:26.850
Gabimaru-san seems rather different now than 
when I first saw him on the beach.

17:27.230 --> 17:30.220
It even looked like he saved you earlier.

17:31.110 --> 17:35.320
Though perhaps that's because 
he must return with a partner.

17:35.510 --> 17:39.070
Don't you have some idea why he's changed?

17:44.870 --> 17:46.330
Stay back.

17:48.010 --> 17:54.350
If any case, I'd feel better if you stayed.

17:54.990 --> 17:57.340
I see...

18:06.640 --> 18:09.360
Are you going to watch me all night?

18:09.900 --> 18:11.480
I'm not sleeping.

18:11.480 --> 18:14.010
I'm taking turns with the other Asaemon.

18:15.740 --> 18:19.110
Then what do the other groups do at night?

18:19.410 --> 18:22.050
The shogunate's plan 
is looking increasingly faulty.

18:22.430 --> 18:24.740
Samurai simply obey.

18:27.000 --> 18:28.240
Then—

18:27.000 --> 18:28.240
Um—

18:30.930 --> 18:31.750
Go ahead.

18:32.370 --> 18:36.170
Just, uh... are you feeling better?

18:36.430 --> 18:37.190
What?

18:37.460 --> 18:39.310
Why are you making that face?

18:39.310 --> 18:41.190
I was just so surprised.

18:41.390 --> 18:44.380
The insects' poison acted quickly

18:44.380 --> 18:46.910
because of the wound I gave you, right?

18:46.910 --> 18:49.290
So I thought I'd, um...

18:50.010 --> 18:52.710
Didn't you say we're short on time?

18:52.710 --> 18:56.780
Well, you know... I had reservations.

18:57.550 --> 18:59.590
And I owe you a favor.

19:00.830 --> 19:02.760
Because of you, I calmed down.

19:02.760 --> 19:04.270
I steeled my resolve.

19:04.920 --> 19:07.690
Rushing in randomly is too dangerous,

19:07.690 --> 19:11.210
and if the Iwagakure are coming, 
then I'd better prepare a counterattack.

19:12.230 --> 19:14.360
I decided I'd live with my wife.

19:14.740 --> 19:17.550
A long life, way longer 
than this job will last.

19:17.890 --> 19:20.580
I won't run from those who try 
to get in my way.

19:20.870 --> 19:23.110
I'll face them head-on.

19:24.630 --> 19:26.070
You're strong.

19:26.710 --> 19:29.280
So are you. Stronger than me.

19:30.410 --> 19:32.190
I-I'm not...

19:32.190 --> 19:33.250
You are.

19:33.250 --> 19:36.250
I'm never wrong about that.

19:36.780 --> 19:41.070
I don't know if it's heart, technique, 
and strength, or influenced by your nature.

19:41.410 --> 19:44.420
At the very least, 
you were strong at the prison.

19:44.670 --> 19:48.670
It wasn't just an impression. 
It's a more practical strength.

19:48.890 --> 19:51.470
I wonder what that feeling was.

19:52.510 --> 19:54.190
You look surprised.

19:54.190 --> 19:55.810
I suppose, yes.

19:56.050 --> 19:59.430
The villagers used to say you 
can't know how strong you are

19:59.430 --> 20:02.310
until you've experienced a lot for yourself.

20:05.270 --> 20:09.170
People understand themselves 
less than we might think.

20:09.170 --> 20:12.910
Until they act, anyway. 
I guess we're all the same.

20:17.190 --> 20:19.990
Nothing showed up.

20:19.990 --> 20:22.830
I guess the monsters aren't active at night.

20:23.070 --> 20:25.660
Sagiri, are you prepared to leave?

20:25.660 --> 20:27.800
I'll escort you to the ship.

20:27.800 --> 20:30.040
I appreciate your consideration.

20:30.250 --> 20:32.040
But I won't be leaving.

20:33.320 --> 20:35.700
If you're worried about 
the rules of the job, then don't.

20:35.700 --> 20:39.800
No, this concerns how I choose to live.

20:39.800 --> 20:43.010
That's ridiculous. You're a woman.

20:43.010 --> 20:46.540
You should return safely 
and bear children for the Yamada clan.

20:47.860 --> 20:50.560
That's what I've always been told.

20:51.150 --> 20:54.880
People regard a woman who wields a sword 
with astonishment and ridicule.

20:55.250 --> 20:57.820
"You're a woman. 
What are you doing?" they'd say.

20:58.100 --> 21:02.220
And more than anything, my father 
sometimes looked at me with disappointment.

21:03.090 --> 21:06.190
A woman can't take over the Yamada clan.

21:06.990 --> 21:08.990
You don't have to push yourself.

21:08.990 --> 21:11.080
Live as a woman.

21:11.440 --> 21:15.750
If I live as a daughter of 
Neck-Chopper Asa, I'm scorned by outsiders.

21:15.750 --> 21:19.510
If I live as a warrior of the Yamada Clan, 
I'm shunned by my family.

21:20.040 --> 21:23.590
If I leave now, it'll follow me 
for the rest of my life.

21:23.840 --> 21:25.670
I don't understand.

21:25.670 --> 21:29.310
It's natural for women 
to have women's responsibilities.

21:30.760 --> 21:34.180
I can't stand to be looked at like that.

21:34.840 --> 21:35.950
What?

21:36.220 --> 21:40.310
Please see me as a samurai.

21:40.310 --> 21:41.480
You...

21:41.830 --> 21:42.830
Please.

21:42.830 --> 21:45.060
Forgive me for defying a senior student

21:45.060 --> 21:47.190
and allow me to live my way.

21:48.890 --> 21:53.330
I know I'm weak and inexperienced, but...

21:53.410 --> 21:56.080
I won't run from those who try 
to get in my way.

21:56.350 --> 22:00.350
But I at least want to decide 
how I'll live for myself.

22:00.710 --> 22:03.090
I'm certain both men and women—

22:03.090 --> 22:09.610
or perhaps all people, 
regardless of status, feel this way.

22:09.810 --> 22:11.560
Please understand.

22:17.350 --> 22:19.310
That was unbearable to listen to.

22:19.310 --> 22:22.120
That isn't how a samurai lives.

22:22.430 --> 22:25.070
This island is like a battlefield.

22:25.070 --> 22:27.360
It's no place for women and children.

22:30.710 --> 22:31.530
What?

22:31.740 --> 22:33.260
When...

22:33.260 --> 22:36.750
Weapons can be procured on the battlefield.

22:37.510 --> 22:40.000
That's what you taught me last night.

22:40.000 --> 22:41.000
How dare you!

22:41.000 --> 22:42.670
A warrior's sword is his soul.

22:42.670 --> 22:44.360
How dare you steal that from me!

22:45.430 --> 22:47.270
G-Genji-dono...
